<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The macOS half of retention-guard.service.

  platform_detect.INSTALL has told every Mac to run

      cp com.tokenusage.retention-guard.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.tokenusage.retention-guard.plist

  since the day that table was written, and this file has never existed in the
  repository. `cp` fails loudly and everything after it is silent: no agent is
  loaded, no tick ever runs, the verify-boot check has no record to find, and
  machine looks exactly like one where the daemon was simply never installed.
  macbook-air-m1 is in the fleet.

  DIFFERENCES FROM THE SYSTEMD UNIT, and why

  KeepAlive with SuccessfulExit=false is launchd's Restart=always. Plain
  <true/> would also restart it after a clean exit, which turns `launchctl
  unload` into a fight.

  ThrottleInterval is RestartSec. launchd's default is 10s and it will refuse
  to respawn faster, logging "service throttled"; 60 matches the unit.

  RunAtLoad is what makes this survive a reboot at all — a LaunchAgent starts
  at login, which on a personal Mac is the equivalent of default.target.

  There is no journal. launchd wants file paths, so output goes to
  ~/Library/Logs, which Console.app reads and `log show` does not. The systemd
  unit deliberately avoids `append:` because one held fd blackholes every tick
  after an `rm`; launchd reopens its output files, so the same hazard does not
  apply here.

  PATHS ARE NOT PORTABLE. /usr/bin/python3 on macOS is the system Python, which
  on some versions is 3.9 — check `python3 -V` and point ProgramArguments at
  Homebrew's if it is older than 3.10. USERNAME must be replaced; launchd does
  not expand ~ or $HOME inside ProgramArguments.

  (A double hyphen cannot appear inside an XML comment, which is why flags are
  written without their leading dashes here. adversarial_platform.py parses
  this file on every run — that is how the first draft was caught, before
  launchctl could reject it on a Mac with a message nobody reads twice. The
  SECOND draft was caught the same way, by writing the offending flag inside
  the sentence warning against it.)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.tokenusage.retention-guard</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/USERNAME/deadreckon-count/retention_guard.py</string>
    <string>--daemon</string>
  </array>

  <!-- ONE daemon, two independent jobs. Set either to 0 to turn that half off
       without touching the other. A disabled job says so on every tick. -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>RETENTION_GUARD_RETENTION</key>
    <string>1</string>
    <key>RETENTION_GUARD_LEDGER</key>
    <string>1</string>
  </dict>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>

  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>60</integer>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/USERNAME/deadreckon-count</string>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/USERNAME/Library/Logs/retention-guard.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/USERNAME/Library/Logs/retention-guard.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
